IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`

-- bgg3-criminal: BGG 2. Abschnitt, Beschwerde in Strafsachen (Art. 78 to 81).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no,
-- tagged FALSE-kind), NOTHING (not covered, tagged NOTHING-kind).  See bgg3-civil for the key.

§ `Art 78 Grundsatz (basic rule)`

-- src:61 | 1 Das Bundesgericht beurteilt Beschwerden gegen Entscheide in Strafsachen.
@ref Art. 78(1) BGG (src:61)
GIVEN `the decision is in a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN           -- Strafsache: not defined in this chapter, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(1) the appeal in criminal matters lies against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is in a criminal matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection reaches only "Entscheide in Strafsachen" and says nothing of other decisions

-- src:62 | 2 Der Beschwerde in Strafsachen unterliegen auch Entscheide über:
-- src:63 | a. Zivilansprüche, wenn diese zusammen mit der Strafsache zu behandeln sind;
@ref Art. 78(2)(a) BGG (src:62-63)
GIVEN `the decision is on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN                                                     -- Entscheid über Zivilansprüche
      `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN            -- zusammen mit der Strafsache zu behandeln
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(2)(a) the appeal in criminal matters also lies against the decision on civil claims` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is on civil claims` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (a) reaches only "Entscheide über ... Zivilansprüche"
        IF `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Zivilansprüche, wenn diese zusammen mit der Strafsache zu behandeln sind" (a failed "wenn": reading (a), for a lawyer; fork F7)

-- src:62 | 2 Der Beschwerde in Strafsachen unterliegen auch Entscheide über:
-- src:64 | b. den Vollzug von Strafen und Massnahmen.
@ref Art. 78(2)(b) BGG (src:62) (src:64)
GIVEN `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- Vollzug von Strafen und Massnahmen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(2)(b) the appeal in criminal matters also lies against the decision on the execution of penalties and measures` MEANS
    IF `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (b) reaches only decisions "den Vollzug von Strafen und Massnahmen"

-- src:62 | 2 Der Beschwerde in Strafsachen unterliegen auch Entscheide über:
-- src:63 | a. Zivilansprüche, wenn diese zusammen mit der Strafsache zu behandeln sind;
-- src:64 | b. den Vollzug von Strafen und Massnahmen.
@ref Art. 78(2) BGG (src:62-64)
GIVEN `the decision is on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(2) the appeal in criminal matters also lies against the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `item (a) answers yes` OR `item (b) answers yes` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `item (a) answers no` THEN JUST FALSE      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Zivilansprüche, wenn diese zusammen mit der Strafsache zu behandeln sind" and no other item holds (fork F7)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unterliegen auch" names items (a) and (b) and does not say no to a decision outside them
    WHERE
        `item (a) answers yes` MEANS
            fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 78(2)(a) the appeal in criminal matters also lies against the decision on civil claims` `the decision is on civil claims` `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter`)
        `item (b) answers yes` MEANS
            fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 78(2)(b) the appeal in criminal matters also lies against the decision on the execution of penalties and measures` `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures`)
        `item (a) answers no` MEANS
            `Art 78(2)(a) the appeal in criminal matters also lies against the decision on civil claims` `the decision is on civil claims` `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:61 | 1 Das Bundesgericht beurteilt Beschwerden gegen Entscheide in Strafsachen.
-- src:62 | 2 Der Beschwerde in Strafsachen unterliegen auch Entscheide über:
-- src:63 | a. Zivilansprüche, wenn diese zusammen mit der Strafsache zu behandeln sind;
-- src:64 | b. den Vollzug von Strafen und Massnahmen.
@ref Art. 78 BGG (src:61-64)
GIVEN `the decision is in a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78 the appeal in criminal matters lies against the decision` MEANS
    IF fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 78(1) the appeal in criminal matters lies against the decision` `the decision is in a criminal matter`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `Art 78(2) the appeal in criminal matters also lies against the decision` `the decision is on civil claims` `the civil claims are to be dealt with together with the criminal matter` `the decision is on the execution of penalties and measures`

§ `Art 79 Ausnahme (exception)`

-- src:67 | Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer des Bundesstrafgerichts, soweit es sich nicht um Entscheide über Zwangsmassnahmen handelt.
@ref Art. 79 BGG (src:67)
GIVEN body IS A `Deciding body`
      `the decision is on coercive measures` IS A BOOLEAN              -- Entscheid über Zwangsmassnahmen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 79 the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of this body` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (body EQUALS `Federal Criminal Court Complaints Chamber`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar reaches only "Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer des Bundesstrafgerichts"
        IF `the decision is on coercive measures` THEN NOTHING          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar applies "soweit es sich nicht um Entscheide über Zwangsmassnahmen handelt"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer des Bundesstrafgerichts, soweit es sich nicht um Entscheide über Zwangsmassnahmen handelt."

§ `Art 80 Vorinstanzen (lower instances)`

-- src:70 | 1 Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen Entscheide letzter kantonaler Instanzen und gegen Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer und der Berufungskammer des Bundesstrafgerichts.[^18]
@ref Art. 80(1) BGG (src:70)
GIVEN body IS A `Deciding body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 80(1) the appeal in criminal matters is admissible against the decision of this body` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `last cantonal instance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Federal Criminal Court Complaints Chamber` THEN JUST TRUE       -- Art 79 narrows this for the Complaints Chamber; each section answers for itself (fork F4)
    WHEN `Federal Criminal Court Appeals Chamber` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "zulässig gegen Entscheide letzter kantonaler Instanzen und gegen Entscheide der Beschwerdekammer und der Berufungskammer des Bundesstrafgerichts" names three bodies and does not close the list with "nur"

-- src:71 | 2 Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein. Diese entscheiden als Rechtsmittelinstanzen. Ausgenommen sind die Fälle, in denen nach der Strafprozessordnung (StPO)[^19] ein oberes Gericht oder ein Zwangsmassnahmengericht als einzige kantonale Instanz entscheidet.[^20]
@ref Art. 80(2) BGG (src:71)
GIVEN `the last cantonal instance is an upper court` IS A BOOLEAN                                                          -- oberes Gericht
      `the last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- als Rechtsmittelinstanz
      `under the Code of Criminal Procedure an upper court or a court for coercive measures decides as the single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN   -- StPO (SR 312.0), outside the sources: asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 80(2) the last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or the exception applies` MEANS
    IF     (`the last cantonal instance is an upper court` AND `the last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance`)
        OR `under the Code of Criminal Procedure an upper court or a court for coercive measures decides as the single cantonal instance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a duty on the cantons ("Die Kantone setzen ... ein"); the text states no consequence for the person if a canton did not comply (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- The cantons' duty in Art 80(2), as a regulative rule.  No time limit is stated and none is invented.
-- src:71 | 2 Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein. Diese entscheiden als Rechtsmittelinstanzen. Ausgenommen sind die Fälle, in denen nach der Strafprozessordnung (StPO)[^19] ein oberes Gericht oder ein Zwangsmassnahmengericht als einzige kantonale Instanz entscheidet.[^20]
@ref Art. 80(2) BGG (the duty) (src:71)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 3` `Cantonal act in chapter 3`
`Art 80(2) the cantons' duty to set up an upper court as last cantonal instance` MEANS
    PARTY Canton
    MUST `set up an upper court as last cantonal instance, deciding as an appeal instance`

§ `Art 81 Beschwerderecht (standing)`

-- src:74 | 1 Zur Beschwerde in Strafsachen ist berechtigt, wer:
-- src:75 | a. vor der Vorinstanz am Verfahren teilgenommen hat oder keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten hat; und
@ref Art. 81(1)(a) BGG (src:74-75)
GIVEN `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN       -- am Verfahren teilgenommen
      `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN         -- keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(a) the person took part before the lower instance or had no chance to` MEANS
    IF `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` OR `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist berechtigt, wer: a. vor der Vorinstanz am Verfahren teilgenommen hat oder keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten hat" (a failed condition of an entitlement: reading (a), for a lawyer)

-- Art 81(1)(b): "ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des
-- angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:" and items 1 to 7.  The items are examples
-- (NOTHING-kind (includes) where an item does not apply); item 4 is repealed.

-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
-- src:77 | 1. die beschuldigte Person,
@ref Art. 81(1)(b)(1) BGG (src:76-77)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(b)(1) the accused person has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` MEANS
    IF person EQUALS `accused person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples; another person is not thereby shown to lack the interest

-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
-- src:78 | 2. ihr gesetzlicher Vertreter oder ihre gesetzliche Vertreterin,
@ref Art. 81(1)(b)(2) BGG (src:76) (src:78)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(b)(2) the legal representative of the accused person has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` MEANS
    IF person EQUALS `legal representative of the accused person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
-- src:79 | 3.[^21] die Staatsanwaltschaft, ausser bei Entscheiden über die Anordnung, die Verlängerung und die Aufhebung der Untersuchungs- und Sicherheitshaft,
@ref Art. 81(1)(b)(3) BGG (src:76) (src:79)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
      `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Anordnung, Verlängerung, Aufhebung der Untersuchungs- und Sicherheitshaft
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(b)(3) the public prosecutor's office has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` MEANS
    IF person EQUALS `public prosecutor's office` AND (NOT `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "ausser bei Entscheiden über die Anordnung, die Verlängerung und die Aufhebung der Untersuchungs- und Sicherheitshaft"; and (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- Item 4 (shown as an ellipsis and repealed by footnote 22): nothing to encode.

-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
-- src:81 | 5.[^23] die Privatklägerschaft, wenn der angefochtene Entscheid sich auf die Beurteilung ihrer Zivilansprüche auswirken kann,
@ref Art. 81(1)(b)(5) BGG (src:76) (src:81)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
      `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Auswirkung auf die Beurteilung der Zivilansprüche
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(b)(5) the private claimant has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` MEANS
    IF person EQUALS `private claimant` AND `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "wenn der angefochtene Entscheid sich auf die Beurteilung ihrer Zivilansprüche auswirken kann"; and (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
-- src:82 | 6. die Person, die den Strafantrag stellt, soweit es um das Strafantragsrecht als solches geht,
@ref Art. 81(1)(b)(6) BGG (src:76) (src:82)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
      `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Strafantragsrecht als solches
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(b)(6) the person who files the criminal complaint has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` MEANS
    IF person EQUALS `person who files the criminal complaint` AND `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "soweit es um das Strafantragsrecht als solches geht"; and (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
-- src:83 | 7.[^24] die Staatsanwaltschaft des Bundes und die beteiligte Verwaltung in Verwaltungsstrafsachen nach dem Bundesgesetz vom 22. März 1974[^25] über das Verwaltungsstrafrecht.
@ref Art. 81(1)(b)(7) BGG (src:76) (src:83)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(b)(7) the federal public prosecutor's office or the administration involved has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` MEANS
    IF person EQUALS `federal public prosecutor's office or the administration involved in an administrative criminal matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
@ref Art. 81(1)(b) BGG (src:76)
GIVEN person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
      `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a legally protected interest in the quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN        -- rechtlich geschütztes Interesse: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1)(b) the person has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` MEANS
    IF     `a listed item applies`
        OR `the person has a legally protected interest in the quashing or change`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist berechtigt, wer: ... b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat" (a failed condition of an entitlement: reading (a), for a lawyer)
    WHERE
        `a listed item applies` MEANS
                fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(b)(1) the accused person has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` person)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(b)(2) the legal representative of the accused person has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` person)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(b)(3) the public prosecutor's office has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` person `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention`)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(b)(5) the private claimant has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` person `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims`)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(b)(6) the person who files the criminal complaint has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` person `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such`)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(b)(7) the federal public prosecutor's office or the administration involved has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` person)

-- src:74 | 1 Zur Beschwerde in Strafsachen ist berechtigt, wer:
-- src:75 | a. vor der Vorinstanz am Verfahren teilgenommen hat oder keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten hat; und
-- src:76 | b. ein rechtlich geschütztes Interesse an der Aufhebung oder Änderung des angefochtenen Entscheids hat, insbesondere:
@ref Art. 81(1) BGG (src:74-76)
GIVEN `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person in a criminal appeal`
      `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a legally protected interest in the quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(1) the person is entitled to appeal in criminal matters` MEANS
    IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(a) the person took part before the lower instance or had no chance to` `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance`)
       AND fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 81(1)(b) the person has a legally protected interest in quashing or changing the decision` person `the decision is on ordering, prolonging or lifting investigative or security detention` `the decision can affect the assessment of the private claimant's civil claims` `the appeal concerns the right to file a criminal complaint as such` `the person has a legally protected interest in the quashing or change`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Zur Beschwerde in Strafsachen ist berechtigt, wer: a. ...; und b. ..." (an entitled-named function: fork F3; Art 81(2) and (3) give other bodies standing, so this answers only the provision's own question)

-- src:84 | 2 Eine Bundesbehörde ist zur Beschwerde berechtigt, wenn das Bundesrecht vorsieht, dass ihr der Entscheid mitzuteilen ist.[^26]
@ref Art. 81(2) BGG (src:84)
GIVEN `the appellant is a federal authority` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                  -- Bundesbehörde
      `federal law provides that the decision is to be communicated to the authority` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- "wenn das Bundesrecht vorsieht, dass ihr der Entscheid mitzuteilen ist"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(2) the federal authority is entitled to appeal in criminal matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appellant is a federal authority` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names only "Eine Bundesbehörde"
        IF `federal law provides that the decision is to be communicated to the authority` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn das Bundesrecht vorsieht, dass ihr der Entscheid mitzuteilen ist" (a failed "wenn" on an entitlement: fork F3)

-- src:85 | 3 Gegen Entscheide nach Artikel 78 Absatz 2 Buchstabe b steht das Beschwerderecht auch der Bundeskanzlei, den Departementen des Bundes oder, soweit das Bundesrecht es vorsieht, den ihnen unterstellten Dienststellen zu, wenn der angefochtene Entscheid die Bundesgesetzgebung in ihrem Aufgabenbereich verletzen kann.
@ref Art. 81(3) BGG (src:85)
GIVEN `the decision is one under Art 78(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is the Federal Chancellery or a federal department` IS A BOOLEAN              -- Bundeskanzlei, Departemente des Bundes
      `the appellant is a subordinate service and federal law provides for its right` IS A BOOLEAN   -- "soweit das Bundesrecht es vorsieht, den ihnen unterstellten Dienststellen"
      `the decision can violate federal legislation in the appellant's field` IS A BOOLEAN         -- Verletzung der Bundesgesetzgebung im Aufgabenbereich
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 81(3) the federal chancellery or department is also entitled to appeal in criminal matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is one under Art 78(2)(b)` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Gegen Entscheide nach Artikel 78 Absatz 2 Buchstabe b"
        IF NOT (`the appellant is the Federal Chancellery or a federal department` OR `the appellant is a subordinate service and federal law provides for its right`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "der Bundeskanzlei, den Departementen des Bundes oder, soweit das Bundesrecht es vorsieht, den ihnen unterstellten Dienststellen"
        IF `the decision can violate federal legislation in the appellant's field` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn der angefochtene Entscheid die Bundesgesetzgebung in ihrem Aufgabenbereich verletzen kann" (a failed "wenn" on an entitlement: fork F3)
